WEBVTT

00:00:01.697 --> 00:00:06.520
Storylines, level one.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:14.746
The Watchers by Jennifer Bassett.

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:24.051
One, the big caves.

00:00:24.111 --> 00:00:29.413
My name is Terrace.

00:00:29.473 --> 00:00:33.856
I am old, 3000 years old.

00:00:33.916 --> 00:00:37.698
I sit here under the palace of Knossos.

00:00:37.758 --> 00:00:40.851
My sister of Keter sits next to me.

00:00:40.911 --> 00:00:45.654
She too is old, 3000 years.

00:00:45.714 --> 00:00:51.208
We do not eat, we drink, and our eyes never close.

00:00:51.268 --> 00:00:54.550
Are we dead or alive?

00:00:54.610 --> 00:01:03.389
It is not important We sit and we wait and we watch for 3,000 years.

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:06.890
We are the watchers.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:15.054
The guard is here too, the guard to Poseidon, guard of the sea stands here in this fall.

00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:20.548
We watch his statue, it is gold, all gold.

00:01:20.608 --> 00:01:34.749
He stands here five meters tall, his arms are gold, His hair is gold, his face is gold, and his gold eyes shine this dark hall.

00:01:34.809 --> 00:01:40.792
We are the swatches.

00:01:40.851 --> 00:01:48.134
Jim and Stella, his sister, are on holiday in Greece.

00:01:48.194 --> 00:01:52.536
They are staying at a hotel in Iraqian on Crete.

00:01:52.596 --> 00:01:55.880
They are talking to their friend, Nikos.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:01.014
Nikos is a Cretan and lives near the Palace of Knossus.

00:02:01.074 --> 00:02:04.046
What are we going to do tomorrow?

00:02:04.106 --> 00:02:05.976
Can we go to Knossus?

00:02:06.036 --> 00:02:07.717
Yes, why not?

00:02:07.777 --> 00:02:14.629
It's a very famous place and very, very old, about 3,000 or 4,000 years old.

00:02:14.689 --> 00:02:16.350
Yes, I'd like to...

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.230
Stella, look at this.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.691
It's about Knossus.

00:02:19.751 --> 00:02:21.242
It's very interesting.

00:02:21.302 --> 00:02:25.138
Caves under Knossus, Eraklian Crete.

00:02:25.198 --> 00:02:29.583
Under the famous palace of Knessus, there are many caves.

00:02:29.643 --> 00:02:35.724
Some of these caves are very big, and some are many, many meters under the ground.

00:02:35.784 --> 00:02:37.675
What is in these caves?

00:02:37.735 --> 00:02:39.205
Nobody knows.

00:02:39.265 --> 00:02:42.046
The caves are very dangerous.

00:02:42.106 --> 00:02:46.046
Next week, Janis Padakis is going to...

00:02:46.106 --> 00:02:48.627
We're going to find these caves, Stella.

00:02:48.687 --> 00:02:50.228
Are you coming with us, Diggos?

00:02:50.288 --> 00:02:51.228
But Jim?

00:02:51.288 --> 00:02:52.389
Yes, yes.

00:02:52.449 --> 00:02:53.780
I'm coming with you.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.652
You can stay with me at my mother's house near Knosses.

00:02:57.712 --> 00:02:58.370
Good.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.548
We're going to need a lot of things.

00:03:00.608 --> 00:03:03.169
Lights and food and water.

00:03:03.229 --> 00:03:04.159
And we need...

00:03:04.219 --> 00:03:06.140
Yes, but it's okay.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.631
I can get everything.

00:03:07.691 --> 00:03:10.512
Jim, the caves are dangerous.

00:03:10.572 --> 00:03:13.274
Yes, but Nickos knows a lot about caves.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:14.844
Yes, I do.

00:03:14.904 --> 00:03:17.946
And I know the palace of Knosses very well.

00:03:18.006 --> 00:03:20.016
Don't forget, I won't there.

00:03:20.076 --> 00:03:22.868
But do you know these caves under Knosses?

00:03:22.928 --> 00:03:24.458
No, I don't.

00:03:24.518 --> 00:03:26.700
But we're going to be careful.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.409
Oh, all right.

00:03:28.469 --> 00:03:29.828
When are we going?

00:03:29.888 --> 00:03:34.119
Tomorrow.

00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:41.171
Sometimes there are lights in these halls and music.

00:03:41.231 --> 00:03:44.031
The people from the palace come down here.

00:03:44.091 --> 00:03:48.382
There are small, quick people with dark eyes and dark hair.

00:03:48.442 --> 00:03:51.983
They bring lights and food and water.

00:03:52.043 --> 00:03:55.094
And they dance the dance of the God.

00:03:55.153 --> 00:03:57.906
They are the God's people.

00:03:57.966 --> 00:04:00.640
No, no, I forget.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.582
They do not come now.

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:08.398
These halls are quiet, dark and quiet.

00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:10.870
It is always night now.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.284
There is no music, no dancing.

00:04:14.344 --> 00:04:20.430
There are no people in the palace now, not after the fire and the water from the sea.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:24.032
They are dead, all dead.

00:04:24.092 --> 00:04:28.595
And we, the Keta and I, sit in the hall of the God.

00:04:28.654 --> 00:04:31.266
We wait, and we watch.

00:04:31.326 --> 00:04:35.348
We are the God's Watchers.

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:45.561
Two.

00:04:45.621 --> 00:04:47.262
The first day.

00:04:47.322 --> 00:04:49.773
At the Palace of Knosses.

00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:52.714
It is seven o'clock in the morning.

00:04:52.774 --> 00:04:56.096
Nickus is looking for the door to the caves.

00:04:56.156 --> 00:04:58.818
Jim and Stella are waiting for him.

00:04:58.878 --> 00:05:01.190
The sun is hot.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.271
I'm thirsty.

00:05:03.331 --> 00:05:05.093
I'm going to drink some water.

00:05:05.152 --> 00:05:06.394
Don't drink a lot.

00:05:06.453 --> 00:05:08.084
We need it in the caves.

00:05:08.144 --> 00:05:09.736
Have we got everything?

00:05:09.796 --> 00:05:10.886
I think so.

00:05:10.946 --> 00:05:12.838
The bags are very heavy.

00:05:12.898 --> 00:05:15.920
Jim, Stella, the door's here.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:16.861
Come on.

00:05:16.921 --> 00:05:23.207
We can go down now.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:29.273
Be careful.

00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:31.165
It's very dark.

00:05:31.224 --> 00:05:32.896
I can't see anything.

00:05:32.956 --> 00:05:33.677
Here.

00:05:33.737 --> 00:05:35.078
Hold this light.

00:05:35.138 --> 00:05:37.310
We need all the lights now.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.613
Walk slowly and be very careful.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.805
Yes, I know.

00:05:42.865 --> 00:05:45.487
How many caves are there?

00:05:45.547 --> 00:05:47.820
This is the tenth cave now.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.862
I can see another one in front of us.

00:05:50.922 --> 00:05:52.083
A long one.

00:05:52.143 --> 00:05:53.694
I'm tired.

00:05:53.754 --> 00:05:56.644
I don't want to look at any more caves today.

00:05:56.704 --> 00:05:58.275
How about some food?

00:05:58.335 --> 00:05:59.285
I'm hungry.

00:05:59.345 --> 00:06:01.566
Yes, let's eat something.

00:06:01.626 --> 00:06:03.556
And we can stay here for the night.

00:06:03.616 --> 00:06:04.477
Good.

00:06:04.537 --> 00:06:05.937
Where's the bag?

00:06:05.997 --> 00:06:07.608
The food is in there.

00:06:07.668 --> 00:06:10.098
How old are these caves, Nikos?

00:06:10.158 --> 00:06:11.109
I don't know.

00:06:11.129 --> 00:06:14.270
3,000 years?

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.370
4,000 years?

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.890
Do many people come to these caves?

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.117
Not many people know.

00:06:20.177 --> 00:06:23.146
Only the old Greek gods.

00:06:23.206 --> 00:06:25.729
The God Poseidon lives in caves.

00:06:25.789 --> 00:06:31.355
Some people say that God Poseidon, there are no old gods in these caves.

00:06:31.415 --> 00:06:33.007
How do you know, Jane?

00:06:33.067 --> 00:06:35.800
The old Greek gods are only stories.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:37.672
We read about them in books.

00:06:37.732 --> 00:06:39.514
They're not important today.

00:06:39.574 --> 00:06:41.157
Oh, yes, they are.

00:06:41.216 --> 00:06:42.698
Don't laugh at them.

00:06:42.758 --> 00:06:45.312
And Poseidon is a dangerous god.

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:47.225
All the books say that.

00:06:47.284 --> 00:06:51.630
He's the God of the sea and the God of earthquakes too.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.162
We have a lot of earthquakes in Greece.

00:06:54.222 --> 00:06:55.443
Don't forget that.

00:06:55.503 --> 00:06:56.764
Oh, Nikos.

00:06:56.824 --> 00:06:58.035
That's silly.

00:06:58.095 --> 00:06:59.866
The God of earthquakes.

00:06:59.926 --> 00:07:01.888
Everybody knows the earthquakes.

00:07:01.948 --> 00:07:02.948
No, Jim.

00:07:03.008 --> 00:07:04.620
Nikos is right.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:09.224
We don't understand everything and don't laugh at the side of them.

00:07:09.284 --> 00:07:13.427
Not here in these caves.

00:07:13.487 --> 00:07:18.560
The years come and the years go.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.798
Three thousand years.

00:07:21.858 --> 00:07:26.356
My sister, Aketa, and I sit and wait.

00:07:26.416 --> 00:07:30.089
It is dark and cold in the hall of the God.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:32.892
The sun never shines here.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.974
Sometimes people come to these halls.

00:07:36.034 --> 00:07:38.056
They are not the God's people.

00:07:38.116 --> 00:07:41.428
They look for gold, only gold.

00:07:41.488 --> 00:07:44.130
And Poseidon is angry.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.932
It is the gold of his people.

00:07:46.992 --> 00:07:51.972
And now it is the God's gold because his people are dead.

00:07:52.032 --> 00:07:58.448
Nobody can take the God's gold or look at the gold face of the God and live.

00:07:58.508 --> 00:08:02.420
But there are no lights, no people now.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:14.483
Only the God Poseidon stands here in this dark hall, God of the blue sea, God of the green sea, God of this dark hall.

00:08:14.543 --> 00:08:20.322
We are His Watchers.

00:08:20.382 --> 00:08:41.524
Three.

00:08:41.584 --> 00:08:44.956
The second day.

00:08:45.016 --> 00:08:48.278
Wake up, Stella.

00:08:48.338 --> 00:08:49.689
Good morning, Nickos.

00:08:49.749 --> 00:08:50.760
Morning.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.174
It's always night in these caves.

00:08:53.234 --> 00:08:54.478
What's the time?

00:08:54.538 --> 00:08:55.708
Seven o'clock.

00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:58.089
Are we going on or back?

00:08:58.149 --> 00:09:00.240
What do you think, Nickos?

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.152
I don't know.

00:09:02.212 --> 00:09:04.122
How many caves are there?

00:09:04.182 --> 00:09:05.983
Fifteen, twenty?

00:09:06.043 --> 00:09:07.084
I don't know.

00:09:07.144 --> 00:09:09.115
But we can look at the next one.

00:09:09.175 --> 00:09:09.945
Or two.

00:09:10.005 --> 00:09:12.876
Four, three, four or five.

00:09:12.936 --> 00:09:14.408
I know you, Jim.

00:09:14.468 --> 00:09:17.949
You want to see everything.

00:09:18.009 --> 00:09:21.842
This is the 14th cave.

00:09:21.902 --> 00:09:23.344
And this cave is big.

00:09:23.404 --> 00:09:24.405
Very big.

00:09:24.465 --> 00:09:25.706
Look.

00:09:25.766 --> 00:09:27.646
This is a road.

00:09:27.706 --> 00:09:29.777
We're walking on a road.

00:09:29.837 --> 00:09:30.578
Yes.

00:09:30.637 --> 00:09:31.708
You're right.

00:09:31.768 --> 00:09:34.429
It's a very old road too.

00:09:34.489 --> 00:09:37.210
Look at these stones on the floor.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.571
Thousands of years old.

00:09:39.631 --> 00:09:41.542
But whose road is it?

00:09:41.602 --> 00:09:43.343
And where does it go to?

00:09:43.403 --> 00:09:44.433
I don't know.

00:09:44.493 --> 00:09:46.064
But we can follow it.

00:09:46.124 --> 00:09:48.325
But it's six o'clock now.

00:09:48.385 --> 00:09:49.125
I think...

00:09:49.145 --> 00:09:49.866
Listen.

00:09:49.926 --> 00:09:51.752
I can hear water.

00:09:51.812 --> 00:09:53.370
Can you hear it?

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:55.620
There's a river in front of us.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.721
We can't get across a river.

00:09:57.781 --> 00:09:59.171
Oh, yes, we can.

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:01.292
I don't want to go across.

00:10:01.352 --> 00:10:02.612
It's dangerous.

00:10:02.672 --> 00:10:03.613
Oh, it isn't.

00:10:03.673 --> 00:10:05.213
Come on, Stella.

00:10:05.273 --> 00:10:07.074
Stella's right.

00:10:07.134 --> 00:10:10.445
Rivers under the ground are dangerous.

00:10:10.505 --> 00:10:11.535
Listen.

00:10:11.595 --> 00:10:13.716
I can hear something.

00:10:13.776 --> 00:10:15.687
It's only the river, Stella.

00:10:15.747 --> 00:10:16.936
It's all right.

00:10:16.996 --> 00:10:21.618
We can go across the river and then we can stop and stay there for the night.

00:10:21.678 --> 00:10:28.352
Yes, we can make a fire and have some food.

00:10:28.412 --> 00:10:33.425
Listen, Sister.

00:10:33.485 --> 00:10:35.566
Do you hear anything?

00:10:35.626 --> 00:10:37.748
There are people at the river.

00:10:37.808 --> 00:10:40.128
They are talking and laughing.

00:10:40.188 --> 00:10:42.260
Listen, Sister.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:46.196
They are coming here to the hall of the God.

00:10:46.256 --> 00:10:47.600
Why?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.373
Who are they?

00:10:49.432 --> 00:10:51.864
What do they want?

00:10:51.925 --> 00:10:53.516
Gold.

00:10:53.576 --> 00:10:55.358
They want gold.

00:10:55.418 --> 00:10:58.060
All people want gold.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:10:59.892
They cannot eat it.

00:10:59.952 --> 00:11:01.562
They cannot drink it.

00:11:01.623 --> 00:11:06.978
But the love of gold is in all men and women too.

00:11:07.038 --> 00:11:10.020
But they cannot take the God's gold.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.631
We are His watchers.

00:11:12.691 --> 00:11:21.822
We call the God, and we say His name, then the God wakes, and His speaks.

00:11:21.882 --> 00:11:36.415
Paul, the third day.

00:11:36.475 --> 00:11:40.929
When are we going to go back?

00:11:40.989 --> 00:11:42.943
This is the third day now.

00:11:43.003 --> 00:11:44.974
I don't like these caves.

00:11:45.034 --> 00:11:46.664
Why not, Stella?

00:11:46.724 --> 00:11:47.805
I don't know.

00:11:47.825 --> 00:11:50.706
I can hear something.

00:11:50.766 --> 00:11:52.286
Or someone.

00:11:52.346 --> 00:11:53.707
It's not the river.

00:11:53.727 --> 00:11:56.298
I want to go back, Nickos.

00:11:56.358 --> 00:11:57.369
Yes.

00:11:57.429 --> 00:12:00.460
Sometimes I can hear something, too.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:03.291
But there's nobody in these caves, Stella.

00:12:03.351 --> 00:12:04.502
Only us.

00:12:04.562 --> 00:12:07.073
Let's look at one more cave.

00:12:07.133 --> 00:12:08.644
Then we can go back.

00:12:08.704 --> 00:12:09.864
Okay?

00:12:09.924 --> 00:12:11.636
What's Jim doing?

00:12:11.696 --> 00:12:12.557
I don't know.

00:12:12.577 --> 00:12:15.140
He's looking at something.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.441
Jim, what are you...

00:12:16.461 --> 00:12:18.042
Hey, look at this.

00:12:18.102 --> 00:12:19.213
It's a bowl.

00:12:19.273 --> 00:12:20.664
A gold bowl.

00:12:20.724 --> 00:12:22.486
It's beautiful.

00:12:22.546 --> 00:12:24.068
Can I hold it for a minute?

00:12:24.088 --> 00:12:26.630
It's very heavy, too.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.762
Look at all this gold.

00:12:28.822 --> 00:12:30.093
Is it old, because?

00:12:30.153 --> 00:12:31.039
Yes.

00:12:31.099 --> 00:12:33.295
Thousands of years old, I think.

00:12:33.355 --> 00:12:34.436
We can sell it.

00:12:34.496 --> 00:12:36.657
We can get a lot of money for this boat.

00:12:36.717 --> 00:12:38.178
We can't do that.

00:12:38.238 --> 00:12:39.369
It's not ours.

00:12:39.429 --> 00:12:40.290
Who is it then?

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.851
It's, well, it's...

00:12:42.871 --> 00:12:43.782
I don't know.

00:12:43.842 --> 00:12:45.383
But it's not ours.

00:12:45.443 --> 00:12:46.694
Don't take it, Jim.

00:12:46.754 --> 00:12:47.734
Leave it here.

00:12:47.794 --> 00:12:48.274
No.

00:12:48.334 --> 00:12:49.546
I'm going to take it.

00:12:49.606 --> 00:12:51.286
It's ours now.

00:12:51.346 --> 00:12:53.968
Can you hear them, sister?

00:12:54.028 --> 00:12:56.270
They are near the hall now.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:57.990
Listen.

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:00.570
They are looking for gold.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.288
Gold.

00:13:02.348 --> 00:13:07.080
All people want gold.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:10.732
Look at that next cave.

00:13:10.792 --> 00:13:12.292
Can you see it?

00:13:12.352 --> 00:13:14.013
It's huge.

00:13:14.073 --> 00:13:15.144
It's not a cave.

00:13:15.204 --> 00:13:15.734
It's a...

00:13:15.794 --> 00:13:16.804
a hole.

00:13:16.864 --> 00:13:18.285
A huge hole.

00:13:18.325 --> 00:13:20.756
Jim, Nikos, don't go in there.

00:13:20.816 --> 00:13:22.046
Why not, Stella?

00:13:22.106 --> 00:13:24.638
I think someone is watching us.

00:13:24.698 --> 00:13:26.498
I don't like it.

00:13:26.558 --> 00:13:28.949
Why don't we go back, please?

00:13:29.009 --> 00:13:31.026
Who is watching us?

00:13:31.086 --> 00:13:33.083
We're the only people here.

00:13:33.143 --> 00:13:34.164
I don't know.

00:13:34.224 --> 00:13:37.717
But someone or something is watching us.

00:13:37.777 --> 00:13:39.468
And it doesn't like us.

00:13:39.528 --> 00:13:41.260
Don't be silly, Stella.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:42.831
Nothing is watching us.

00:13:42.891 --> 00:13:45.523
Come on.

00:13:45.583 --> 00:13:49.796
I can see them now, sister.

00:13:49.856 --> 00:13:51.878
Two men and a woman.

00:13:51.938 --> 00:13:53.410
They are young.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.922
Two of them have blue eyes.

00:13:55.982 --> 00:13:58.404
They are not people from the palace.

00:13:58.464 --> 00:14:02.084
They are not the gods' people.

00:14:02.144 --> 00:14:05.343
And they cannot come in here.

00:14:05.403 --> 00:14:08.094
They cannot take the God's gold.

00:14:08.154 --> 00:14:14.766
They cannot look at the face of the God.

00:14:14.826 --> 00:14:19.228
Look at those statues there.

00:14:19.288 --> 00:14:21.949
They're very, very old.

00:14:22.009 --> 00:14:23.630
I don't like them.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:25.220
Look at their eyes.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:27.241
Come away, Stella.

00:14:27.301 --> 00:14:30.282
I can see something at the end of a hole.

00:14:30.342 --> 00:14:31.402
Look.

00:14:31.462 --> 00:14:32.954
What is it?

00:14:33.014 --> 00:14:36.078
It's tall, very tall.

00:14:36.138 --> 00:14:41.152
It's a statue, a huge statue, and it's shining.

00:14:41.212 --> 00:14:43.104
It's gold.

00:14:43.164 --> 00:14:44.936
Oh, gold.

00:14:44.996 --> 00:14:46.518
Don't look at it.

00:14:46.578 --> 00:14:48.090
Don't go in there.

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.321
Please, Jim.

00:14:49.381 --> 00:14:50.152
Please.

00:14:50.212 --> 00:14:51.514
It's dangerous.

00:14:51.574 --> 00:14:52.604
Stop him, Nick.

00:14:52.664 --> 00:14:54.464
I'll stop him.

00:14:54.524 --> 00:14:57.425
They are looking into the hall now.

00:14:57.485 --> 00:14:59.226
Call the god.

00:14:59.286 --> 00:15:00.846
Now, sister.

00:15:00.906 --> 00:15:02.097
Now.

00:15:02.157 --> 00:15:04.718
Save the name of the god.

00:15:04.778 --> 00:15:06.910
They cannot come in.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:10.821
They cannot come in.

00:15:10.881 --> 00:15:13.012
Shh.

00:15:13.072 --> 00:15:14.483
Be quiet for a minute.

00:15:14.543 --> 00:15:15.504
Wait, Jim.

00:15:15.564 --> 00:15:16.404
Listen.

00:15:16.464 --> 00:15:17.224
Why?

00:15:17.284 --> 00:15:17.955
What's...

00:15:18.015 --> 00:15:18.885
Shh.

00:15:18.945 --> 00:15:20.836
I think Stella's right.

00:15:20.896 --> 00:15:22.127
There's something...

00:15:22.167 --> 00:15:23.054
Listen.

00:15:23.114 --> 00:15:24.450
Because...

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:25.611
what's that?

00:15:25.671 --> 00:15:26.681
Can you hear it?

00:15:26.741 --> 00:15:27.502
Oh no!

00:15:27.562 --> 00:15:28.242
No!

00:15:28.302 --> 00:15:29.892
The ground is moving!

00:15:29.952 --> 00:15:31.593
It's an earthquake!

00:15:31.653 --> 00:15:33.774
There's going to be an earthquake!

00:15:33.834 --> 00:15:35.235
The stones are falling!

00:15:35.295 --> 00:15:35.845
Run!

00:15:35.905 --> 00:15:36.495
Run!

00:15:36.555 --> 00:15:37.656
Back to the river!

00:15:37.716 --> 00:15:38.286
Run!

00:15:38.346 --> 00:15:39.166
Quick Stella!

00:15:39.226 --> 00:15:39.917
Run!

00:15:39.977 --> 00:15:40.827
Run!

00:15:40.887 --> 00:15:42.788
We can't!

00:15:42.808 --> 00:15:44.239
The walls are falling!

00:15:44.299 --> 00:15:46.089
Everything is falling!

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:47.310
We can't get out!

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:55.852
We can't get out!

00:15:55.912 --> 00:16:06.686
Crete News, 14th of August.

00:16:06.746 --> 00:16:09.478
Earthquake at Knosses.

00:16:09.538 --> 00:16:12.711
Three young people are dead.

00:16:12.771 --> 00:16:15.613
Eraklian Crete.

00:16:15.674 --> 00:16:20.388
Anna Stavros, mother of Nicos Stavros says.

00:16:20.448 --> 00:16:28.934
Nicos and his two English friends, Jim and Stella, are in the caves under the Palace of Knosses.

00:16:28.994 --> 00:16:32.260
But where is the door to the caves?

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:36.396
Nobody can find it now after the earthquake.

00:16:36.456 --> 00:16:40.068
My son and his friends cannot get out.

00:16:40.128 --> 00:16:42.700
They are dead.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:47.932
The God Poseidon, God of the sea is angry.

00:16:47.992 --> 00:16:52.896
He speaks and the ground moves and the stones fall.

00:16:52.956 --> 00:16:57.028
But the God can sleep again now, Assistant.

00:16:57.088 --> 00:16:59.929
The men and the woman are quiet.

00:16:59.989 --> 00:17:01.996
They cannot move.

00:17:02.056 --> 00:17:04.514
They lie under the stones.

00:17:04.574 --> 00:17:15.389
They hold the God's gold bowl in their hands, but they cannot go back across the river, and they cannot look at the face of the God.

00:17:15.449 --> 00:17:31.366
The God's gold eyes shine in this dark hall with lifeless watches.

00:17:31.426 --> 00:17:42.200
